    "significance": "User acceptance and perception are critical bottlenecks for neurotechnology adoption. This study gathers qualitative input from potential BCI recipients on surgical implantation, helping developers understand patient priorities, fears, and expectations around invasive brain implants. Such insights are essential for designing patient-centered clinical trials and informed consent processes, and they guide research priorities to ensure that neurotechnology advances address real clinical needs and patient values."
